[{"short_id":"n5jtzr","created_at":"2026-11-16T13:19:20.113-06:00","title":"Where did the ACK go?","url":"https://yashgarg.dev/posts/where-did-the-ack-go/","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eBreaking things with JioFiber, SIP and Asterisk.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Breaking things with JioFiber, SIP and Asterisk.","submitter_user":"yashgarg","user_is_author":true,"tags":["networking","reversing"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/n5jtzr","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/n5jtzr/where_did_ack_go"},{"short_id":"lcy32t","created_at":"2026-11-16T12:54:27.961-06:00","title":"Formal Operations Specifications for Reliable System Management","url":"https://djapg7v42ea9q.cloudfront.net/pdf/hotnets26-final281.pdf","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eAbstract: Large-scale production systems are largely operated by management software like Kubernetes operators and increasingly by AI agents. Production systems have diverse functionalities, interfaces, and fault-tolerance properties; hence, their management semantics are complex and less standard. Today, management-plane software is largely implemented based on experience and documents of the managed systems, where correct management is a best effort.\nWe advocate for the practice of writing formal operations specification (FOS) as a formal contract to precisely describe expected behaviors of the production system and to enable systematic checking and verification of management-plane software and agents. We argue that the FOS should be part of standard system interface to enable reliable system management. We suggest that every production system include a FOS and share our experience of writing FOSes for real-world systems; we show that writing and maintaining a FOS is affordable and can potentially be automated\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Abstract: Large-scale production systems are largely operated by management software like Kubernetes operators and increasingly by AI agents. Production systems have diverse functionalities, interfaces, and fault-tolerance properties; hence, their management semantics are complex and less standard. Today, management-plane software is largely implemented based on experience and documents of the managed systems, where correct management is a best effort.\r\nWe advocate for the practice of writing formal operations specification (FOS) as a formal contract to precisely describe expected behaviors of the production system and to enable systematic checking and verification of management-plane software and agents. We argue that the FOS should be part of standard system interface to enable reliable system management. We suggest that every production system include a FOS and share our experience of writing FOSes for real-world systems; we show that writing and maintaining a FOS is affordable and can potentially be automated","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["formalmethods","pdf"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lcy32t","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lcy32t/formal_operations_specifications_for"},{"short_id":"s7mejx","created_at":"2026-11-16T12:17:29.216-06:00","title":"How Rust Changed Me As A Developer","url":"https://blog.startifact.com/posts/how-rust-changed-me/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"faassen","user_is_author":true,"tags":["performance","rust"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/s7mejx","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/s7mejx/how_rust_changed_me_as_developer"},{"short_id":"6t3oi4","created_at":"2026-11-16T11:56:45.490-06:00","title":"On Leaving Swift for Rust","url":"https://www.prux.org/posts/goodbye-swift-hello-rust/","score":2,"flags":2,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"marcprux","user_is_author":true,"tags":["mobile","rust","swift"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6t3oi4","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6t3o